WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:07.000
Imagine you see a car crash. One researcher asks how fast the cars hit.

00:00:07.000 --> 00:00:14.000
Another asks how fast they smashed. One word changes the question.

00:00:14.000 --> 00:00:21.000
In 1974, researchers found that answers changed too. A week later, some recalled broken glass.

00:00:21.000 --> 00:00:28.000
But no broken glass appeared in the film. This is a study of memory reports.

00:00:28.000 --> 00:00:35.000
It is not proof a recording changes your brain. Ask what was observed and actually tested.

00:00:35.000 --> 00:00:42.000
The offer can wait. The evidence comes first.
